            "presentation_state": "show_all",
            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "Gives the value that appears most often, and where it appears. Use it to smooth a stream of labels: the most common gesture class over the last 15 frames is a steadier answer than any one frame's guess. Also for the most common note, colour index or state.\n\nSYNTAX:\nt.mode <dim>\nWithout a dim, along the last dim (each row of a matrix gets its own). With one, dim and\nkeep_dims boxes appear.\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\ntensor in:\nThe values. Every input sends.\n\ndim, keep_dims (also inlets; only when a dim was given):\nThe dim counted along, and whether to keep it as size 1.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nmode:\nThe most common value. Of several equally common, the smallest.\n\nindices:\nA position where it appears. Sent first.\n\nThe answer stays on the input's device: a tensor on the GPU is worked on there and comes out there. On the Mac's GPU (mps), torch has no mode: it is done on the CPU and the answer moved back.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\n3 1 3 2 3 1: 3 appears three times, more than any other.\n\nRELATED:\nt.unique counts every value. t.bincount counts whole numbers. t.median is the middle value, not the most common one. t.rolling_buffer collects the last frames to vote over.",
                    "value_type": "str"
                },
                "1": {
                    "name": "lock",
                    "value": true,
                    "value_type": "bool"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "width",
                    "value": 760,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "3": {
                    "name": "height",
                    "value": 900,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "4": {
                    "name": "text_size",
                    "value": "30",
                    "value_type": "str"
                }
            },
            "text": "Gives the value that appears most often, and where it appears. Use it to smooth a stream of labels: the most common gesture class over the last 15 frames is a steadier answer than any one frame's guess. Also for the most common note, colour index or state.\n\nSYNTAX:\nt.mode <dim>\nWithout a dim, along the last dim (each row of a matrix gets its own). With one, dim and\nkeep_dims boxes appear.\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\ntensor in:\nThe values. Every input sends.\n\ndim, keep_dims (also inlets; only when a dim was given):\nThe dim counted along, and whether to keep it as size 1.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nmode:\nThe most common value. Of several equally common, the smallest.\n\nindices:\nA position where it appears. Sent first.\n\nThe answer stays on the input's device: a tensor on the GPU is worked on there and comes out there. On the Mac's GPU (mps), torch has no mode: it is done on the CPU and the answer moved back.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\n3 1 3 2 3 1: 3 appears three times, more than any other.\n\nRELATED:\nt.unique counts every value. t.bincount counts whole numbers. t.median is the middle value, not the most common one. t.rolling_buffer collects the last frames to vote over."
        },
